{
  "row": {
    "id": "q5",
    "scenario": "Learning v2 L3 fixture: a learned change to a note the user saved or edited is a suggestion (a candidate carrying supersedes) that retires nothing until a user-directed confirm bound to the target's revision; a learned change to a learned note is an automatic replacement whose withdrawal brings the old note back; a suggestion is never archived and never edited by a tool call",
    "required_outcome": "S1–S5, S9, S10 and ForgetMode::Withdraw of design 09 §3.2–§3.3 hold at the file layer: G2 still refuses an active replacement of a `user` note from any surface the user did not direct."
  },
  "design": [
    "09 §3.1 the rule, case by case; §3.2 S1–S5, S9, S10; §3.3 withdraw and forget; ruling LR9, LR12",
    "03 §4 origins and G2; §6 derived supersession (a candidate supersedes nothing)",
    "03 §7c R9: a suggestion never enters the same-fact_key group"
  ],
  "loads_in": ["slice-2"],
  "notes_for_implementer": "File-layer only: `store` is `Partition::create` with the context's actor, `update` is `Partition::update`, `withdraw` is `Partition::forget_as(.., ForgetMode::Withdraw)`, `forget` is the plain forget. The extractor's decision (design 09 §2.5) is not here: each store names its policy. X is the user's saved commute note, L a learned editor note, E a hand-dropped (`external`) style guide, S a learned note citing the same message (2502) as the suggestions and the automatic replacement — a sibling whose sources a withdrawal must not suppress. The service's S6 dismissals and S7 are the service tests', not this file's: after step 13 the second suggestion b2 is still a pending candidate here. Owner decision LQ11 (design 03 §4, rev 7.4; 09 rev 3.33): `alice_tool` here is the file layer's direct policy (`ReplacePolicy::Direct`), so a `ModelTool` supersede or edit of the `user` note is still `authority_conflict` at this layer; on the service's tool path the same supersede, and an edit that changes the note's content, is written as a suggestion instead (`memory/service/tool_suggestion_tests.rs`).",
